course: dictionary
lesson: 8571
title: Scenery: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scenery is a noun, and it is uncountable, so you say some scenery, not a scenery. Its first meaning is the natural features of a place, like hills, rivers, trees and sky, especially when they are beautiful.
explain: Read this sentence: «Behind the stage is a hidden team: the stage crew, dressed in black so you hardly notice them, move scenery, run the lights and sound, and help actors change costumes in seconds.» The words stage, lights and actors are clues. This is a theatre, so scenery means the painted backgrounds and objects that show where the play is happening.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could the crew really move real hills and rivers between scenes? No, so the theatre meaning fits. A third meaning is an idiom: «a change of scenery» means going somewhere different for a rest or a new start.
fact: Scenery is uncountable: say some scenery, not a scenery.
fact: «Scenery» means the natural features of a place, like hills, rivers, trees and sky, especially when beautiful.
fact: In a theatre, scenery means the painted backgrounds and objects on a stage that show where the play is happening.
fact: «A change of scenery» means going somewhere different for a rest or a new start.
fact: Useful phrases: beautiful scenery, stunning scenery, part of the scenery.
exercise: In «the stage crew move scenery», what does scenery mean? | The lights that shine on the actors | The costumes the actors wear | The natural features of a place, like hills and rivers | *The painted backgrounds and objects on a stage that show where the play is happening
exercise: Which phrase means going somewhere different for a rest or a new start? | *A change of scenery | Stunning scenery | Part of the scenery | Beautiful scenery
exercise: Choose the right word: The ___ with its hills and lakes was stunning. | audience | costume | ticket | *scenery
test: Is scenery countable? Choose the right answer. | Yes, you say two sceneries | No, you can never use it with some | Yes, you say a scenery | *No, you say some scenery, not a scenery
test: Which sentence uses scenery to mean natural features? | *The train ran through beautiful scenery of mountains and lakes | The actors changed their scenery before the show | Ella painted the scenery for the school play | The stage crew moved the scenery in seconds
exam: Read this: «The stage crew move scenery between the scenes.» What does scenery mean, and which clue helps you? | *Painted backgrounds on the stage, because of the words stage crew and scenes | Real hills and rivers, because of the word move | A kind of food, because of the word stage | A pair of shoes, because of the word crew
